  "consts": [
   "core/self_heal.py - turn a blank-but-present field into a healed value AND a\nback-patched, re-cacheable recipe anchor.\n\nWhy this exists\n---------------\nV2's cached path is zero-AI: a stored ``PoRecipe`` of regex anchors replays over\nthe PDF and any field the anchor misses stays blank. That is the \"漏抓→留空\"\nbehaviour. This module is the safety net:\n\n  1. detect anchor fields that parsed to blank while their human-readable LABEL\n     is clearly present in the document (proof the data exists and the anchor\n     simply missed it - not that the PO lacks the field);\n  2. ask the model ONCE, for just those fields (core.ai.focus_extract);\n  3. fill the parsed ``PurchaseOrder`` (never overwrite a value that is already\n     correct);\n  4. when the model's value round-trips through ``synthesize_field_anchor``,\n     patch the recipe anchor and write it back to the fingerprint cache, so the\n     NEXT PO of this layout is caught by regex - no more AI for that field.\n\nOnly runs on the CACHED path (caller gates it). When no field is missing-with-\nlabel it returns immediately and costs ZERO AI, so the normal fast path is\nuntouched. When offline it also no-ops. There is no loop: the back-patched\nrecipe is cached for future files; this file's ``po`` is already filled.\n",
